  "markdown_vectors_doc": "D3 follow-up (fixture 28's last gap): a raw HTML block in MARKDOWN renders on both lanes, sanitised. Server: md_to_tiptap. Client: mdToHtml then htmlToNote. `md` in, `shape` out, the same shape spelling as above.",
  "markdown_vectors": [
    {"name": "an unclosed div block", "md": "x\n\n<div>b]]", "shape": "doc(paragraph('x'), paragraph('b]]'))"},
    {"name": "a div block interrupting a paragraph", "md": "see\n<div>b]] end\n\nafter", "shape": "doc(paragraph('see'), paragraph('b]] end'), paragraph('after'))"},
    {"name": "two div lines in one block", "md": "<div>a</div>\n<div>b</div>\n\ntail", "shape": "doc(paragraph('a'), paragraph('b'), paragraph('tail'))"},
    {"name": "a script block is dropped with its content", "md": "<script>alert(1)</script>\n\nok", "shape": "doc(paragraph('ok'))"},
    {"name": "a comment block is nothing", "md": "<!-- c -->\n\nok", "shape": "doc(paragraph('ok'))"},
    {"name": "inline tags inside a block", "md": "<div><b>bold</b> text</div>", "shape": "doc(paragraph('bold', ' text'))"},
    {"name": "markdown between an opening and a closing div", "md": "<div>\n\n*md* inside\n\n</div>", "shape": "doc(paragraph('md', ' inside'))"},
    {"name": "a table block", "md": "<table><tr><td>t</td></tr></table>", "shape": "doc(table(tableRow(tableCell(paragraph('t')))))"},
    {"name": "a paragraph block", "md": "<p>para</p>", "shape": "doc(paragraph('para'))"},
    {"name": "difference 2: a details whose markdown body spans blocks", "md": "<details>\n<summary>S</summary>\n\nbody *em*\n\n- li\n\n</details>\n\nafter", "shape": "doc(toggle(toggleSummary('S'), toggleContent(paragraph('body ', 'em'), bulletList(listItem(paragraph('li'))))), paragraph('after'))"},
    {"name": "difference 2: an aside whose markdown body spans blocks", "md": "<aside>\n\nnote **b**\n\n</aside>\n\nafter", "shape": "doc(callout(paragraph('note ', 'b')), paragraph('after'))"},
    {"name": "difference 2: an unclosed details holds the rest", "md": "<details>\n<summary>S</summary>\n\nbody\n\nno close", "shape": "doc(toggle(toggleSummary('S'), toggleContent(paragraph('body'), paragraph('no close'))))"},
    {"name": "difference 2: a one-line details", "md": "<details><summary>S</summary>one line</details>\n\nafter", "shape": "doc(toggle(toggleSummary('S'), toggleContent(paragraph('one line'))), paragraph('after'))"},
    {"name": "difference 2: nested details across blocks", "md": "x\n\n<details>\n<summary>A</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>B</summary>\n\ninner\n\n</details>\n\nouter\n\n</details>\n\nz", "shape": "doc(paragraph('x'), toggle(toggleSummary('A'), toggleContent(toggle(toggleSummary('B'), toggleContent(paragraph('inner'))), paragraph('outer'))), paragraph('z'))"}
  ],
  "block_node_vectors_doc": "D3 follow-up (difference 2): <aside> is a callout and <details> a toggle on both lanes, with the same attrs. `html` in (HTML through html_to_tiptap / htmlToNote), `shape` out, and `attrs`: one string per callout or toggle in document order, `callout emoji=<default|other> variant=<value>` or `toggle open=<value>`. The leading-emoji split is pinned per lane (an emoji is never written raw into this file).",
  "block_node_vectors": [
    {"name": "an aside with no emoji", "html": "<aside>plain aside</aside>", "shape": "doc(callout(paragraph('plain aside')))", "attrs": ["callout emoji=default variant=null"]},
    {"name": "an aside of paragraphs", "html": "<aside><p>para</p><p>two</p></aside>", "shape": "doc(callout(paragraph('para'), paragraph('two')))", "attrs": ["callout emoji=default variant=null"]},
    {"name": "an empty aside", "html": "<aside></aside>", "shape": "doc(callout(paragraph))", "attrs": ["callout emoji=default variant=null"]},
    {"name": "a details with a summary and a paragraph", "html": "<details><summary>Sum</summary><p>body</p></details>", "shape": "doc(toggle(toggleSummary('Sum'), toggleContent(paragraph('body'))))", "attrs": ["toggle open=true"]},
    {"name": "a details with bare body text", "html": "<details><summary>Sum</summary>body text</details>", "shape": "doc(toggle(toggleSummary('Sum'), toggleContent(paragraph('body text'))))", "attrs": ["toggle open=true"]},
    {"name": "a details with no summary", "html": "<details><p>no summary</p></details>", "shape": "doc(toggle(toggleSummary, toggleContent(paragraph('no summary'))))", "attrs": ["toggle open=true"]},
    {"name": "a closed details still imports open, its summary marked", "html": "<details><summary>S <b>b</b></summary>x</details>", "shape": "doc(toggle(toggleSummary('S ', 'b'), toggleContent(paragraph('x'))))", "attrs": ["toggle open=true"]},
    {"name": "a details inside an aside", "html": "<aside><details><summary>T</summary><p>in</p></details></aside>", "shape": "doc(callout(toggle(toggleSummary('T'), toggleContent(paragraph('in')))))", "attrs": ["callout emoji=default variant=null", "toggle open=true"]}
  ],
  "unsafe_image_vectors_doc": "D3 follow-up (difference 1): a raw <img> whose src the policy refuses as UNSAFE leaves the same visible notice on both lanes, never a silent drop. Server: md_to_tiptap(md, unsafe_image_notice=True), its importNotice nodes. Client: parseImport with the generic adapter, htmlToNote, each image's media item failure (its name, else the image's alt). `notices` = [reason, name] in document order.",
  "unsafe_image_vectors": [
